  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "QR traceability path",
      "items": [
        "QrCard encodes the current-domain /trace/{batchCode} URL.",
        "Camera or image scan extracts the URL/code and navigates to that route.",
        "The route resolves the code against SAMPLE_BATCHES; it does not query the chain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "On-chain vs off-chain",
      "items": [
        "Registry storage includes batch metadata hash, creator, time, weight, status, recall flag, parent IDs, and latest lab-document hash.",
        "Contract events also carry lifecycle fields such as lab result/type, package lot hash/count, custody actors/location, and recall reason.",
        "Ponder persists selected batch, lab-test, and recall event projections; the app PostgreSQL schema is defined but unused by current routes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What is not wired today",
      "items": [
        "Dashboard create/recall actions change React state and the in-memory sample map; they do not submit contract transactions.",
        "Viem/Wagmi, Supabase Auth helpers, and Drizzle are configured, but no current app route calls them.",
        "Certificate hashing happens in the browser; no document upload/blob-storage call is implemented."
      ]
    }
  ]
